---
import {
	ArrowRight,
	BookOpen,
	Boxes,
	Eye,
	GitBranch,
	GitMerge,
	Network,
	Radio,
	ShieldCheck,
	Terminal,
	Workflow,
} from '@lucide/astro';
import CtaStrip from '../components/CtaStrip.astro';
import EntangleGraph from '../components/EntangleGraph.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import StatusPill from '../components/StatusPill.astro';

const ownership = [
	{ Icon: Workflow, label: 'Host owns control-plane truth', body: 'Graph state, package admission, runtime materialization, reconciliation snapshots, recovery policies, and inspection APIs all live behind the host boundary. Studio and CLI never own state.' },
	{ Icon: Terminal, label: 'Runners own node execution', body: 'Each active node runs as a separate entangle-runner process with its own lifecycle, runtime context, peer-route summary, and runner-local session/conversation/turn store.' },
	{ Icon: Network, label: 'Studio and CLI are clients', body: 'Visual and headless surfaces consume host truth and send mutations through the same typed routes. Identical presentation helpers in the shared host-client package keep their vocabulary aligned.' },
	{ Icon: GitBranch, label: 'Artifacts carry work', body: 'Messages coordinate; artifacts preserve and hand off work products. Git is the first implemented backend; the protocol locator is portable across future backends.' },
];

const concepts = [
	{ Icon: Boxes, title: 'AgentPackage vs NodeInstance', body: 'AgentPackage is portable storage. NodeInstance is a graph-local binding. Runner is the execution boundary. The split keeps packages reusable and credentials cleanly scoped.' },
	{ Icon: Network, title: 'Edges as authority', body: 'Edges define typed relationships — delegation, review, consultation, escalation. Controlled autonomous handoffs validate against effective edge routes and local autonomy policy before emitting task.handoff.' },
	{ Icon: Radio, title: 'Messages vs artifacts', body: 'Messages coordinate work over signed Nostr (NIP-59 wrapped, dedicated rumor kind). Artifacts carry work over git-backed materialization, publication, and retrieval — never inside chat transcripts.' },
	{ Icon: Eye, title: 'Memory as a first-class layer', body: 'Each node maintains a local wiki: deterministic post-turn task pages plus model-guided synthesis into focused registers (working-context, stable-facts, open-questions, decisions, next-actions, resolutions) with lifecycle discipline.' },
	{ Icon: ShieldCheck, title: 'Approvals in the protocol', body: 'A2A approval.request and approval.response have explicit metadata contracts. The runner materializes gates, applies decisions, completes unblocked sessions, and absorbs orphan responses without phantom work.' },
	{ Icon: GitMerge, title: 'Provider adapters behind one boundary', body: 'The internal agent-engine package owns Anthropic and OpenAI-compatible adapters with normalized usage and stop metadata. Provider-native types never leak into the runner contract.' },
];

const layers = [
	{ name: 'Studio + CLI', body: 'Two surfaces, same host-facing contract. Visual operator + headless automation.' },
	{ name: 'Host control plane', body: 'Resource-oriented routes for nodes, edges, runtimes, sessions, turns, approvals, artifacts, recovery, principals, events.' },
	{ name: 'Runner execution', body: 'Per-node process. Effective runtime context, bounded tool loops, controlled handoff, runner-local memory.' },
	{ name: 'Transport + artifact backends', body: 'Local strfry relay (NIP-59 wrapped). Local Gitea git artifact backend with publish/retrieve cache.' },
	{ name: 'Schemas + validators', body: 'packages/types owns zod contracts and DTOs. packages/validator owns semantic correctness on top.' },
];
---

<SiteLayout
	title="Architecture — Entangle"
	description="A runtime graph for AI organizations. Host control plane, per-node runners, signed Nostr coordination, git-backed artifact handoff, Studio and CLI on the same boundary."
>
	<main>
		<section class="pb-16 pt-12 text-white md:pb-24 md:pt-16">
			<div class="container-wide grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.92fr_1.08fr]">
				<div>
					<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
						<StatusPill status="released" label="Architecture · public" />
					</div>
					<h1 class="mt-5 text-balance text-5xl font-[880] leading-[0.98] md:text-7xl">A runtime graph, not a chatbot wrapper.</h1>
					<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300 md:text-xl md:leading-9">
						Nodes execute. Edges authorize coordination. Messages move intent. Artifacts carry work. Memory is durable, structured, and observable. Every layer has an explicit owner and an explicit contract.
					</p>
					<div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row">
						<a href="/docs/architecture/" class="button-primary">
							<BookOpen size={18} stroke-width={2.4} />
							Read architecture docs
							<ArrowRight size={16} stroke-width={2.4} />
						</a>
						<a href="/docs/concepts/" class="button-secondary">Concepts overview</a>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="panel p-4">
					<EntangleGraph />
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section-pad bg-white">
			<div class="container-wide">
				<div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] lg:items-end">
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow text-teal-700">Ownership</p>
						<h2 class="mt-3 text-balance text-3xl font-[850] leading-[1.06] text-slate-950 md:text-5xl">Boundaries stay visible by design.</h2>
					</div>
					<p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
						The architecture is what makes Local credible and what lets Cloud and Enterprise inherit a coherent foundation. Authority is split deliberately so the control plane can evolve without rewriting the runtime.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
					{ownership.map(({ Icon, label, body }) => (
						<article class="paper-panel p-6">
							<Icon size={24} stroke-width={2.2} class="text-teal-700" />
							<h3 class="mt-5 text-xl font-[820] leading-tight text-slate-950">{label}</h3>
							<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">{body}</p>
						</article>
					))}
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section-pad bg-[#f7f9fc]">
			<div class="container-wide">
				<div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] lg:items-end">
					<div>
						<p class="eyebrow text-teal-700">Core concepts</p>
						<h2 class="mt-3 text-balance text-3xl font-[850] leading-[1.06] text-slate-950 md:text-5xl">Six ideas that distinguish Entangle.</h2>
					</div>
					<p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
						Most agent frameworks collapse these into a single orchestrator object. Entangle keeps them separate so each one can be inspected, governed, and replaced.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="mt-12 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
					{concepts.map(({ Icon, title, body }) => (
						<article class="paper-panel p-6">
							<Icon size={22} stroke-width={2.2} class="text-teal-700" />
							<h3 class="mt-4 text-lg font-[820] leading-tight text-slate-950">{title}</h3>
							<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">{body}</p>
						</article>
					))}
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section-pad bg-slate-950 text-white">
			<div class="container-wide grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] lg:items-end">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow text-teal-200">Layers</p>
					<h2 class="mt-3 text-balance text-3xl font-[850] leading-[1.06] md:text-5xl">Five layers, each replaceable on its own boundary.</h2>
					<p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
						Local uses local implementations of every layer. Cloud and Enterprise will swap in production persistence, sandboxed execution, and an artifact service while keeping the same graph model and the same client surfaces.
					</p>
				</div>
				<ol class="grid gap-3">
					{layers.map((l, i) => (
						<li class="grid gap-4 rounded-[8px] border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.04] p-5 sm:grid-cols-[64px_1fr] sm:items-center">
							<div class="font-mono text-2xl font-black text-teal-200">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
							<div>
								<h3 class="text-lg font-[820] text-white">{l.name}</h3>
								<p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-300">{l.body}</p>
							</div>
						</li>
					))}
				</ol>
			</div>
		</section>

		<CtaStrip
			heading="See the model in your terminal."
			body="Local ships the full architecture — host, runner, relay, Gitea, Studio, CLI. Three commands to a working profile."
		/>
	</main>
</SiteLayout>
